course(u,'我提过的那位朋友',['Identify a friend through meaningful descriptions','Recognize four phrase structures','Read a subject–predicate phrase as the larger predicate'],[
('本领','ability; skill','năng lực','noun','她有组织活动的本领。','She has the ability to organize events.','本领要看实际做了什么。','Ability depends on what was actually done.'),
('本事','ability; capability','bản lĩnh','noun','他修东西很有本事。','He is good at repairing things.','有本事也可以请别人帮忙。','A capable person can still ask for help.'),
('长处','strength; strong point','điểm mạnh','noun','她的长处是听得认真。','Her strength is listening carefully.','先说长处，再说需要练的地方。','Name strengths before areas needing practice.'),
('短处','weakness; shortcoming','điểm yếu','noun','我的短处是说得太急。','My weakness is speaking too hastily.','短处不是整个人的评价。','A weakness is not an assessment of the whole person.'),
('成熟','mature','trưởng thành','adjective','她处理问题很成熟。','She handles problems maturely.','成熟不等于从来不问问题。','Maturity does not mean never asking questions.'),
('程度','degree; extent','mức độ','noun','我们练到的程度不同。','We have practised to different levels.','先问了解的程度，再介绍。','Ask how much is understood before explaining.'),
('表面','surface; appearance','bề mặt','noun','表面安静，不代表没在想。','A quiet appearance does not imply not thinking.','只看表面还不够。','Looking only at appearances is insufficient.'),
('表明','to show; indicate','cho thấy','verb','她的回答表明她看过通知。','Her response indicates she read the notice.','这句话表明时间还没确定。','This sentence indicates the time is still unconfirmed.'),
('显得','to seem; appear','có vẻ','verb','换个说法，介绍显得自然一些。','A different phrasing makes the introduction seem more natural.','停一下，语气显得不那么急。','A pause makes the tone seem less rushed.'),
('显示','to display; show','hiển thị','verb','屏幕显示的是文章标题。','The screen displays the article title.','先看显示的日期。','Check the displayed date first.'),
('形象','image; impression','hình tượng','noun','介绍不能只说外在形象。','An introduction should not only describe outward image.','她给人的形象很可靠。','The impression she gives is reliable.'),
('形式','form; format','hình thức','noun','这篇介绍用对话的形式。','This introduction takes the form of dialogue.','形式可以换，事实别改。','The format may change; do not alter the facts.'),
('文字','written language; text','chữ viết','noun','文字写得简短，意思清楚。','The written text is short and clear.','先核对文字，再录音。','Check the written text before recording.'),
('文章','article; written piece','bài viết','noun','这篇文章介绍一位朋友。','This article introduces a friend.','文章内容由她自己确认。','She confirms the article’s content herself.'),
('读者','reader','độc giả','noun','读者不一定认识她。','Readers do not necessarily know her.','给读者说明你们在哪里见过。','Tell readers where you met.'),
('写作','writing','viết văn','noun','写作前先问她愿不愿意。','Ask whether she agrees before writing.','写作不是替别人定性。','Writing is not defining somebody else’s character for them.'),
('杂志','magazine','tạp chí','noun','她给杂志写了短文。','She wrote a short piece for the magazine.','杂志还没刊登这篇介绍。','The magazine has not yet published this introduction.'),
('现实','reality; actual life','thực tế','noun','现实里的朋友和故事人物不同。','Real-life friends differ from fictional characters.','回到现实，先问她的意见。','Return to reality and ask her opinion first.'),
('班级','class; class group','lớp học','noun','我们在同一个班级认识。','We met in the same class.','班级不同也可以一起练习。','People from different classes can practise together.'),
('保安','security guard; security','bảo vệ','noun','门口的保安帮我们找到了教室。','The guard at the entrance helped us find the classroom.','先向保安说明来意。','Explain the purpose of the visit to the guard first.'),
('职业','occupation','nghề nghiệp','noun','她愿意介绍自己的职业。','She is willing to introduce her occupation.','职业不是人的全部。','An occupation is not a person’s whole identity.'),
('评价','assessment; to assess','đánh giá','noun','评价要说具体事情。','An assessment should name concrete things.','她不同意这个评价，先听原因。','She disagrees with this assessment; hear the reason first.')],
[grammar(u,'三32','介宾 / 方位 / 兼语 / 同位短语','Recognize what connects the phrase',
'介宾: 跟朋友 / 在教室, preposition plus its object. 方位: 桌子上 / 教室里面, referent plus location word. 兼语: 请朋友介绍, where 朋友 is both the object of 请 and the subject of 介绍. 同位: 老师张先生, where two expressions identify the same person. Do not interpret apposition as two teachers or a pivot construction as two unrelated events.',[
('我跟朋友在教室里面见面。','I meet my friend inside the classroom.'),('请朋友介绍她的长处。','Ask the friend to introduce her strengths.'),('老师张先生也来了。','Teacher Mr Zhang also came.')],
('老师张先生是两个人。','老师张先生指同一个人。','The two appositive expressions refer to the same person.')),
grammar(u,'三53','大主语 + 小主语 + 谓语','Read the larger topic and its internal statement',
'A subject–predicate phrase can itself be the predicate: 她汉语说得很流利. 她 is the larger subject; 汉语说得很流利 says something about her Chinese. Similarly 这篇文章内容很清楚 has 这篇文章 as the larger subject and 内容很清楚 as its predicate. This is not a request to add a comma or 是 between every pair of nouns.',[
('她汉语说得很流利。','She speaks Chinese fluently.'),('这篇文章内容很清楚。','This article’s content is clear.'),('他组织活动的本领很强。','His ability to organize events is strong.')],
('她是汉语说得很流利。','她汉语说得很流利。','Do not add 是 to this ordinary subject–predicate construction.'))],
('The friend in the introduction','Identify the friend and what is actually known about her.',[
('你提过的那位朋友，是我们班级里的那位吗？','Is the friend you mentioned the one in our class?'),('对。她汉语说得很流利，写作也有本领。','Yes. She speaks Chinese fluently and has writing ability.'),('我只看过她的文章，表面上显得很安静。','I have only read her article; she seems quiet on the surface.'),('表面不能代替评价。她处理活动很成熟。','Appearance cannot replace assessment; she handles events maturely.'),('她的职业是什么？杂志上没有写。','What is her occupation? The magazine did not state it.'),('这个先问她。介绍的形式可以换，事实得确认。','Ask her first; the introduction’s format can change, but facts need confirmation.'),('那请她介绍自己的长处和短处。','Then ask her to introduce her own strengths and weaknesses.'),('好，老师张先生也可以听，但让她先说。','Okay; teacher Mr Zhang can listen too, but let her speak first.')],
[('mainidea','What should the introduction distinguish?',['Confirmed facts and impressions','Occupation and inevitable personality','Two people named teacher Zhang'],0),('detail','Where did the speakers meet the friend?',['In their class','At a hospital','At an airport'],0),('inference','Does a quiet appearance establish her whole personality?',['No','Yes','Only in a magazine'],0)],[],True),
('A description with a basis','Read how the draft is checked with its subject.',[
('写作开始前，读者需要知道这位朋友是谁，不能只看屏幕显示的名字。','Before writing, readers need to know who this friend is, beyond the displayed name.'),('我们在班级认识，门口的保安帮过忙，这些是可以确认的事情。','We met in class and the entrance guard helped us; these are confirmable events.'),('她汉语说得很流利，文章内容很清楚；这两句各有一个内部主谓结构。','She speaks Chinese fluently and the article’s content is clear; each contains an internal subject–predicate structure.'),('她的本领和本事要看实际做过的事，了解的程度也要说明。','Her abilities should be judged from actual actions, and the extent of our knowledge stated.'),('认真观察作品，评价具体长处与短处；基础还在练，不等于没有能力。','Observe the work carefully and assess specific strengths and weaknesses; still practising foundations does not mean having no ability.'),('成熟是这次处理问题给人的形象，不是对所有未来行为的保证。','Maturity is the impression from this handling of a problem, not a guarantee of all future behaviour.'),('文字的形式改变不了现实，杂志介绍的事实由她自己确认。','A text’s format cannot change reality; she confirms the facts in the magazine introduction.'),('她的回答表明职业暂时不写，也让介绍显得更尊重本人。','Her response indicates the occupation will be omitted for now, making the introduction more respectful.')],
[('mainidea','What supports the description?',['Specific events and the friend’s confirmation','Only a displayed name','Invented future guarantees'],0),('detail','What is omitted for now?',['Her occupation','Every written word','All reference to class'],0),('inference','Is practicing foundations incompatible with ability?',['No','Yes','Only for readers'],0)],[(4,'长处'),(6,'形式')],False),
('The introduction is hers','Read an original drama scene.',[
('你写我很安静，我刚才还在讨论呢。','You wrote that I am quiet; I was just discussing things.'),('我只看到表面，介绍写得太满了。','I saw only the surface and overstated the introduction.'),('长处短处，我自己说。职业这次先不写。','I will state my strengths and weaknesses; omit my occupation this time.'),('好。文章写你，不替你做决定。','Okay. The article describes you; it does not decide for you.')],
[('inference','What does the author change?',['Overconfident claims and occupation disclosure','The friend’s actual job','The original meeting place'],0)],[],True),
dict(tf=[('表面','表面安静，不代表没在思考。','A quiet appearance does not imply not thinking.','The person is certainly not thinking.',False,'Appearance does not establish the private state.'),('职业','她确认这次先不写职业。','She confirms her occupation should be omitted this time.','The occupation should be disclosed now.',False,'The explicit choice is omission.')],reply=[('评价','只看过一篇文章，可以评价所有行为吗？','Can one article establish all behaviour?',['不可以，要说具体事情。','安静就是从不讨论。','职业就是全部人格。'],0,'Restrict the claim to evidence.'),('班级','你们在哪认识？','Where did you meet?',['在同一个班级。','读者就是两个老师。','表面就是职业。'],0,'State the actual meeting context.')],fill=[('文字','先核对文字，再录音。','Check the written text before recording.'),('读者','读者不一定认识她。','Readers do not necessarily know her.')],match=[('文章',[('这篇文章内容很清楚。','The article’s content is clear.'),('她汉语说得很流利。','She speaks Chinese fluently.'),('老师张先生也来了。','Teacher Mr Zhang also came.')]),('本领',[('她有组织活动的本领。','She can organize events.'),('请朋友介绍长处。','Ask the friend to introduce strengths.'),('桌子上的作品是她的。','The work on the table is hers.')])]),
[('Ask before describing','这句介绍，你愿意这样写吗？','Would you like this introduction written this way?','Allow correction and omission.'),('Separate observation','这是我的印象，不一定完整。','This is my impression; it may be incomplete.','State the limits of your knowledge.')],
[('她的长处是什么？','What is her strength?','State one observed ability',['她组织活动很有本领。']),('能写她的职业吗？','May I write her occupation?','Ask the person first',['先问她愿不愿意。'])],
'Native check: 本领 versus 本事 register, apposition 老师张先生, larger-topic scope in 主谓谓语句, 职业 disclosure, 表面 impressions versus evidence, and 作品评价 phrasing. Native review pending.')

